[[Steelcase]], 2004. Designed by Glen Oliver Löw with Steelcase's own designers and IDEO.

An office chair made to come apart. Steelcase says it can be taken to pieces in about five minutes with common hand tools, and that up to 95% of it can be recycled.

Steelcase also calls it the first product ever to be [[Cradle to Cradle]] certified.

The metal goes one way and the plastic goes another. No [[Monstrous Hybrid]]. See [[Design for Disassembly]].

Compare the [[Aeron Chair]], ten years older, and the [[Catifa Carta]].

[[By intent or by habit?]] By intent, and they wrote it on the box.

Sources:

* [[Think (Steelcase product sheet, PDF)|https://www.steelcase.com/content/uploads/sites/10/2015/03/Think_EN.pdf]]: designer credits, five-minute disassembly
* [[Think (Steelcase Singapore)|https://sg.steelcase.com/products/think-scarlet-edition]]: common hand tools, up to 95% recyclable, first Cradle to Cradle certification
